# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# KCD 60x2 gameplay, 5.3 min recorded locally on the release policy, b:vsync -src 60 -lock -lag 75 -etw -dejit 2026-09-23 (first C++17 build, f662417); loading and exit trimmed. Lock pull wraps, and one game hitch that releases the lock into a 118-present blend run
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description KCD 60x2 gameplay, 5.3 min recorded locally on the release policy, b:vsync -src 60 -lock -lag 75 -etw -dejit 2026-09-23 (first C++17 build, f662417); loading and exit trimmed. Lock pull wraps, and one game hitch that releases the lock into a 118-present blend run
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 118
field_long_runs 2
field_synth_pct 1.1
field_pull_wraps 6
#
# WHAT IT COVERS: the lock wrap again, and a hitch that releases the lock. From about 47 s to
# 135 s the pull sat within about 1 ms of the wrap point and wrapped back and forth across the
# comb/16 band's edge: a repeat at 48.07 s (inside the replay's warmup, so not counted), skips at
# 88.35, 112.93 and 135.10 s, repeats at 96.62 and 128.70 s, and one more skip at 326.57 s,
# inside the blend run below. Each one is on screen in the local recording at frame precision
# (log = video + 50.27 s: the two repeats fixed the offset, then all four skips landed on the
# frames it predicted). Then, at about 324 s, a game hitch (a 45 ms capture gap, 37 ms in the
# game's own flips) drops the lock; it re-engages and slews its pull from 14.5 ms to 2.3 ms at
# about 104 us a present, blending the whole way: runs of 56 and 118 presents. max_worst_run
# pins that run, the item-5 class of long blend run after a lock release at a small hitch.
#
# WINDOW. KCD loads into gameplay with capture stalls until log 46.8 s, and the exit starts at
# 364.9 s. Cut 47.5 s to 364 s: every relay hold, blocked present and capture gap over 50 ms in
# the log falls outside it.
#
# FIDELITY. Replay 1.3% / runs 2 / worst 118 / pull wraps 6 against field 1.1% / runs 2 / worst
# 118 / pull wraps 6; the dejitter arm, which is how the relay ran, reads 1.1% / 2 / 118, exact.
# Each replayed wrap lands within one present of the field's. That holds
# only at the capture's own lag: replayed without the 75 ms of extra lag, the pull sits half a
# source period away, the wraps happen at other moments, and the worst run reads 62.
#
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. max_pull_wraps is one of the two numbers this fixture is for, max_worst_run
# the other.
max_worst_run 118
max_long_runs 2
max_synth_pct 1.7
min_reseeds 0
max_pull_wraps 6
src_hint 60.0
extra_lag_ms 75
arrivals 37309
